Public domain dedication
========================

This submission was prepared for the McGill-FIAM Asset Management Hackathon
2026. The competition rules state that a hackathon submission is public domain
and free, and that what is evaluated is the idea and the backtest behind it
rather than any technology claim. This file records that accordingly.

To the extent possible under law, the authors dedicate all copyright and
related and neighbouring rights in this code, its documentation and the
accompanying deck to the public domain worldwide. The work is distributed
without any warranty. Where a public domain dedication is not legally
effective, any person may use, copy, modify and distribute the work for any
purpose, commercial or otherwise, without condition.

This dedication covers the code in this repository, the generated submission
artefacts and the deck. It does not cover the competition's own datasets or
the third-party market data referenced by the pipeline, which remain subject
to the terms under which they were supplied and are not redistributed here.

If the organisers prefer a conventional permissive licence instead, the rules
name Apache-2.0 as an acceptable example; replacing the text above with the
Apache-2.0 licence text would satisfy the same requirement.
